As you hand over the powerful Dagger of Vengeance you can't help but
wonder if you are being played for a fool. You have traveled all over the
world running dangerous tasks and barely survived this last one. Yet all
you have to show for it is empty promises and a handful of gold.
~
#38825
Quest for Th dagger part 5: Quest for a dark indigo dagger named Bittertongue and head of Thief of Lore in CoH~
As you enter the dark, cavernous room once again you wonder why you
are doing this. You are one of the best thieves in the business. Yet here
you are running dangerous errands. You think about turning around and
walking away but decide to give the ancient figure one more chance to
be straight with you.

'There is a legendary thief that makes her home in the Cavern of Heroes. 
Yes, she is even better than you think you are. Over the centuries she has 
stolen the knowledge and secrets of countless wise men and sorcerers. And 
with that knowledge she has created a most unusual dagger. For your next quest, 
bring me her precious dagger so I may study it. I don't care how you go
about getting her dagger. Just do it!'
~
Find a way into the Cavern of Heroes and return with the dagger from the Thief of Lore.
~
45 60 142614488 200 30 45
G 38814
P 38824
O OBJ 35032
R GOLD 7
You hand over the dark indigo dagger named Bittertongue and wait expectantly.
Surely now you are done. You have spent much time learning how to gain 
entry to the Cavern of Heroes and watched some of your companions die in the
attempt to gain this dagger.

The ancient figure barely looks up as you enter. 'Leave the dagger over there
in the usual spot.' You wait expectantly for something more, but the ancient
figure acts like you are not even there. You storm from the room resolving that
you are done running quests for this mad man.
~
#38826
Quest for Th dagger part 6: Quest for the Blazing Eyes of Txachamitxchual~
After storming from the room the last time you ran a near fatal errand for the
unusual figure apparently imprisoned in the guild, you decided to do a little
research on your own. Using up several valuable favors and blackmailing 
the right people, you were able to discover some of the most famous thieves
in history had dealings with that creature but that lesser thieves had given up
in disgust. You think you may be on to something and determine that you
will continue to see these foolhardy missions though and see what game the
ancient being is really playing.

The now familiar figure looks down from contemplating the ceiling as you
enter his hidden room. 'About time you returned. Your next task is waiting
for you. The Priest King of Xchantharus has looked into the face of chaos
itself, and while it has driven him mad, it has also imbued him with very
unusual and great powers. Go and slay him and bring me his head and eyes, 
so that I might know what he has seen!'
~
Fight your way to the Priest King of Xchantharus and retrieve his head
and eyes. You know this will not be an easy task.
~
45 60 142614488 200 30 45
G 38814
P 38825
O MOB 31500
O OBJ 31503
R EXP 13
You return covered in gore and hand over the head of the Priest King of 
Xchantharus dripping with blood. Within the sunken face the eyes still glow
a deep red with their own inner light. You hope to never again see a place gone 
as mad as the land you just left.

The mysterious figure plucks the eyes from the severed head you brought him
and somehow inserts them into his own eye sockets. He looks around with eyes
that now glow the same fierce red as they did when you last saw them in the 
Priest King's head. 'Amazing! To think that he was able to see so much and not
die instantly! 'He looks over at you and trails off in a thoughtful 'Hmmmm...'
before looking away. 'You may go now!'
~
#38827
Quest for Th dagger part 7: Retrieve a Shimmering Cube~
As you enter the familiar room of stone, the ancient chained figure
looks up at you with a look you have not seen before. In the past he
had looked insane and barely there. Now his eyes pierce right through
you and you sense an awful power and intelligence behind them. You
can believe those stories that this being might indeed be an ancient god.

'You have completed the tasks I set before you. You have shown true
cunning and skill as a thief with no assurances of any reward for risking
your life. I have one final task for you and then I shall give you a reward
that will aid you in your adventures and be an example of your skill to
those who matter. But to make that item I need an object of great power
called a shimmering cube. It is protected by a magical guardian that
wanders this world and hides in dangerous places to protect the
cube. Bring the cube to me, and you shall have your reward.'
~
Search the land for the mysterious guardian and return with a shimmering 
cube of power.
~
45 60 134225880 50 30 45
G 38814
P 38826
O OBJ 18198
R OBJ 38850
You hand over the shimmering cube of power that you took from the
corpse of the dead guardian you spent months tracking down. The
power of the cube is obvious as it seems to distort the very fabric of
reality around it.

The ancient figure pulls out the various daggers of power you had
given him and carefully places them in the cube of power. 'The 
heads were for my own collection, but these daggers combined with
the pure chaos of the eyes of Xchantarus and the magic of the cube
will create an object of incredible power.'

There is a brilliant &14flash&00 that temporarily blinds you! As your sight
the black flag you see the ancient figure holding out a shimmering dagger
to you. As you take the dagger you can feel the power running through
the hilt and down the blade. 'This is for the amusement you have
provided me and the determination you showed when lesser thieves
would have given up.' With that the figure turns from you and resumes
the pose he seems to favor. You have no doubts now that the rumors
were true and this ancient god does indeed stay just to cause mischief
and not due to any chains forged by mortal hands. Shaking your head
with wonder you leave the room and the being that almost got you killed
several times. 
~
